<h1>trailmap</h1>
<p class="muted">The task domain, served by Rails — RFCs, stories and the
ready queue, read and written in one place.</p>

<h2>Pages</h2>
<div class="box">
  <div class="box-row"><a href="<%= rfcs_path %>">RFCs</a> — every RFC and its stories.</div>
  <div class="box-row"><a href="<%= backlog_path %>">Backlog</a> — the ready queue, in rank order.</div>
  <div class="box-row"><a href="<%= dashboard_path %>">Fleet</a> — open PRs, panes, spawns and CI, live from ringo.</div>
</div>

<h2>Owners</h2>
<p class="muted">The same work, the GitHub way: an owner, its repositories, and
code, issues, pull requests, actions, projects, wiki, insights and settings
under each one.</p>
<div class="box">
  <% if @owners.empty? %>
    <div class="empty">No owner is configured. <code>bin/rails db:seed</code> writes them.</div>
  <% end %>
  <% @owners.each do |owner| %>
    <div class="box-row"><a href="<%= owner_path(owner.login) %>"><%= owner.login %></a>
      <% if owner.display_name.present? %> — <%= owner.display_name %><% end %></div>
  <% end %>
</div>

<h2>Status vocabulary</h2>
<p class="muted">Story statuses, then the RFC statuses that gate them.</p>
<p>
  <% %w[draft ready claimed in-progress blocked done closed].each do |status| %>
  <%= render "shared/status_badge", status: status %>
  <% end %>
</p>
<p>
  <%= render "shared/status_badge", status: "active" %>
  <%= render "shared/status_badge", status: nil %>
</p>
